# PDF Viewer Code Explanation - Step by Step

This is a **lazy-loading PDF viewer** that renders pages only when they're near the viewport to save memory. Let me break it down:

---

## **Step 1: Initial Setup &amp; Imports**

```javascript
import * as pdfjsLib from "https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/pdf.js/5.4.149/pdf.min.mjs";
pdfjsLib.GlobalWorkerOptions.workerSrc = "https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/pdf.js/5.4.149/pdf.worker.min.mjs";
```

**What happens:**
- Loads the PDF.js library from CDN
- Sets the worker thread (handles heavy PDF processing)

**DOM Setup:**
```javascript
const pdfInput = document.getElementById("pdfInput");        // File input
const clearBtn = document.getElementById("clearBtn");        // Clear button
const pdfContainer = document.getElementById("pdfContainer"); // Where pages go
const loading = document.getElementById("loading");          // Loading spinner
const error = document.getElementById("error");              // Error messages
const pdfInfo = document.getElementById("pdfInfo");          // PDF info box
```

---

## **Step 2: User Selects a PDF File**

```javascript
pdfInput.addEventListener("change", async function () {
    const file = this.files[0];
    if (!file) return;
```

**Example Input:**
```
User clicks file input → Selects "invoice.pdf" (2.5 MB)
```

**Step 2a: Validation**

```javascript
if (file.type !== "application/pdf" &amp;&amp; !file.name.toLowerCase().endsWith(".pdf")) {
    showError("Please select a valid PDF file.");
    return;
}
```

**Example Output:**
```
✓ File "invoice.pdf" passes validation (type = "application/pdf")
✗ File "document.txt" fails → Error shown to user
```

---

## **Step 3: Clear Previous State**

```javascript
clearViewer();  // Reset everything
showError("");
error.classList.add("d-none");  // Hide errors
showLoading(true);              // Show loading spinner
```

**DOM Before:**
```html
<div id="pdfContainer">
  <!-- Old PDF pages still here -->
</div>
```

**DOM After:**
```html
<div id="pdfContainer">
  <!-- Now empty -->
</div>
<div id="loading">
  <div class="spinner-border"></div> <!-- Visible now -->
</div>
```

---

## **Step 4: Read File &amp; Load PDF**

```javascript
const arrayBuffer = await file.arrayBuffer();
const loadingTask = pdfjsLib.getDocument({ data: arrayBuffer });
currentPDF = await loadingTask.promise;
```

**Example Log Output:**
```javascript
console.log(currentPDF);
// Output:
// {
//   numPages: 45,
//   fingerprint: "8a3b2c1d4e5f6a7b",
//   pdfVersion: "1.4",
//   ...
// }
```

---

## **Step 5: Display PDF Information**

```javascript
pdfName.textContent = file.name;      // "invoice.pdf"
pageCount.textContent = currentPDF.numPages;  // "45"
pdfInfo.classList.remove("d-none");   // Show info box
```

**DOM Output:**
```html
<div id="pdfInfo">
  <strong>File:</strong> invoice.pdf
  <strong>Pages:</strong> 45
</div>
```

**Console Output:**
```
✓ Loaded: invoice.pdf (45 pages)
```

---

## **Step 6: Create Page Placeholders**

```javascript
await createPagePlaceholders(currentPDF);
```

This creates a `<div>` for **every page** immediately (not rendering the canvas yet).

**Example: Creating Page 1-3 (of 45)**

```javascript
// Iteration 1:
pageElement = <div class="pdf-page" data-page="1">
  <div class="pdf-page-wrapper">
    <div class="pdf-placeholder">
      <spinner> Loading page 1...
    </spinner></div>
    <div class="page-number">Page 1</div>
  </div>
</div>

// Iteration 2:
pageElement = <div class="pdf-page" data-page="2">
  <div class="pdf-page-wrapper">
    <div class="pdf-placeholder">
      <spinner> Loading page 2...
    </spinner></div>
    <div class="page-number">Page 2</div>
  </div>
</div>

// Iteration 3:
pageElement = <div class="pdf-page" data-page="3">
  <!-- ... -->
</div>

// After 10 pages: await setTimeout(0)  ← Yield to browser
// Continues for all 45 pages...
```

**DOM After:**
```html
<div id="pdfContainer">
