## **Step 7: Setup Intersection Observer**

```javascript
setupPageObserver();
```

This creates an **IntersectionObserver** that watches when pages come within **800px** of the viewport.

**Example Setup:**
```javascript
pageObserver = new IntersectionObserver(callback, { rootMargin: "800px 0px" });

// Observe all pages:
document.querySelectorAll(".pdf-page").forEach(page =&gt; {
    pageObserver.observe(page);
});
```

**Visual Representation:**
```
┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│         Viewport (window)           │
│  ┌───────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │   Currently visible           │  │
│  └───────────────────────────────┘  │
└─────────────────────────────────────┘
      ↑ 800px margin above
┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│   Page 2 (not yet visible) ← Observer triggers here
└─────────────────────────────────────┘
```

---

## **Step 8: User Scrolls - Page Becomes Visible**

User scrolls down, Page 2 enters the 800px margin:

```javascript
// Observer callback fires:
if (entry.isIntersecting) {
    pageObserver.unobserve(pageElement);  // Stop watching this page
    const pageNumber = Number(pageElement.dataset.page); // "2"
    renderPage(currentPDF, pageNumber, pageElement);
}
```

**Console Output:**
```
Page 2 is intersecting → Rendering...
```

