## **Step 10: Render Page (Canvas)**

```javascript
async function renderPage(pdf, pageNumber, pageElement) {
    const page = await pdf.getPage(pageNumber);  // Get page 2
    const viewport = getViewport(page);          // { width: 918, height: 1188 }
    
    const wrapper = pageElement.querySelector(".pdf-page-wrapper");
    const placeholder = wrapper.querySelector(".pdf-placeholder");
    placeholder.remove();  // Remove spinner
    
    const canvas = document.createElement("canvas");
    canvas.width = 918;
    canvas.height = 1188;
    
    wrapper.prepend(canvas);  // Add blank canvas
    
    await page.render({
        canvasContext: canvas.getContext("2d"),
        viewport: viewport
    }).promise;  // Draw the PDF on canvas
}
```

**DOM Before Rendering:**
```html
<div class="pdf-page-wrapper">
  <div class="pdf-placeholder">
    <spinner> Loading page 2...
  </spinner></div>
  <div class="page-number">Page 2</div>
</div>
```

**DOM After Rendering:**
```html
<div class="pdf-page-wrapper">
  <canvas width="918" height="1188">
    <!-- PDF content drawn here -->
  </canvas>
  <div class="page-number">Page 2</div>
</div>
```

**Console Output:**
```
✓ Rendered page 2 (918×1188px)
```

