## **Full Flow Diagram**

```
USER PICKS FILE
     ↓
[Validate] ← Check if .pdf
     ↓
[Clear] ← Remove old pages
     ↓
[Load] ← Read file → ArrayBuffer → PDF.js
     ↓
[Display Info] ← Show filename &amp; page count
     ↓
[Create Placeholders] ← All 45 pages as empty divs with spinners
     ↓
[Setup Observer] ← Watch for pages entering viewport
     ↓
USER SCROLLS (page 2 enters 800px margin)
     ↓
[Render] ← getPage() → getViewport() → Create Canvas → Render on Canvas
     ↓
[Show Canvas] ← Remove spinner, display PDF page
     ↓
CONTINUE SCROLLING
     ↓
[Repeat for all pages as needed]
```

---

## **Key Performance Features**

| Feature | Benefit |
|---------|---------|
| **Placeholders First** | Scroll height correct immediately |
| **Lazy Rendering** | Only renders pages near viewport |
| **Intersection Observer** | Efficient, native API |
| **Yield Every 10 Pages** | Keeps browser responsive |
| **Scale Clamping** (0.5-1.5) | Balanced readability |
| **Unobserve After Render** | Pages don't re-render when scrolling back |

This design means a 100-page PDF loads instantly with placeholders, but only renders pages the user actually views!


